⍝ Run the Jarvis session tests from the shell:
⍝     dyalogscript Tests/Sessions/run.apls
⍝ Loads Source/Jarvis.dyalog (relative to this script) unless JARVIS_SOURCE names another copy,
⍝ uses ports from JARVIS_TEST_PORT (default 8491) up, runs #.test_Sessions.Run, prints any failures, and exits with 0 if every test passed, 1 otherwise.
⎕IO←1
here←{⊃1 ⎕NPARTS ⍵}⊃{⍵/⍨∨/¨'run.apls'∘⍷¨⍵}2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
src←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'JARVIS_SOURCE'
src←(1+0∊⍴src)⊃src(here,'../../Source/Jarvis.dyalog')
⎕←'Jarvis source: ',src
{}#.⎕FIX'file://',src
{}#.⎕FIX'file://',here,'test_Sessions.apln'
{0∊⍴⍵:⍬ ⋄ #.test_Sessions.BasePort←¯1+⊃⊃(//)⎕VFI ⍵}2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'JARVIS_TEST_PORT'
failures←#.test_Sessions.Run
⎕←''
⎕←(⍕≢failures),' failure(s)'
⎕←⍪failures
⎕OFF(0≠≢failures)
